{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Aaron took Elisheva, the daughter of Amminadav, the sister of Nachshon.</b> Just as Scripture mentioned the mother of the prophets (i.e., the wife of Moses) for their honor, and to say that she is the daughter of Levi, a righteous man, and there is a hint that a miracle was performed for her, so too it mentioned the mother of the priesthood, that she is of distinguished lineage from the seed of royalty, the sister of the great prince. And it mentioned the mother of Pinchas, who is also a priest who earned it on his own (Zevachim 101a). And if Putiel were a name that is not interpreted, what reason would there be to mention the name of a man about whom we do not know who he is? Therefore our Sages said (Bava Batra 110a; Sotah 43a) that he was from the seed of Yosef, who <b>pityey</b> (suppressed) his inclination, and from the seed of Yitro, who <b>pitem</b> (fattened) calves for idol worship, and he was mentioned in praise, that they merited through their righteousness to eternal priesthood. And by way of the plain sense, it may be said that the verses mention the names of the mothers of kings: \"and the name of his mother was Ma'acha daughter of Avishalom\" (I Kings 15:2, 10), \"and the name of his mother was Azuva daughter of Shilchi\" (II Chronicles 20:31), and so all of them; or else Putiel was honored and well-known in his generation, and Scripture mentioned him in praise. And the verse says <b>of the daughters of Putiel</b> (Elohim's kohen), and does not say \"the daughter of Putiel,\" because he had many daughters and he (Eleazar) chose one of them; or she was not his daughter but rather his granddaughter, traced to him on account of his eminence, and therefore Scripture did not mention her name."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The citation 'Elohim's kohen' appears to refer to the phrase in Exodus, identifying Putiel's daughters with Eleazar's wife; I have rendered it as it reads. The wordplay on פיטם/פיטפט is preserved with parenthetical glosses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:03:55.431746550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}